---
import Layout from '../../layouts/AssetsLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;

import { SEQUENCES as seqs } from '../../data/emails';
---
<Layout title="Email Nurture Sequences | Thyme4Sleep" description="The Thyme4Sleep free-to-paid email sequences.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:860px;text-align:center;">
      <div>
        <span class="pill tool">Content studio</span>
        <h1 style="margin-top:18px;">Email Nurture Sequences</h1>
        <hr class="divider" style="margin-inline:auto;" />
        <p class="lead" style="margin-inline:auto;">Four sequences in Georgia’s voice: free download → paying family, and Calm Nights family → results, a review, or the right 1:1 package. Paste them into your email platform and set the delays and rules shown. Sequences 3 and 4 need a platform with link-click tagging and conditional automations (Kit or MailerLite both do this).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {seqs.map(([id, title, note, emails]) => (
    <section class="band" id={id} style="padding-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="narrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">{title}</span>
        <p class="muted">{note}</p>
        {emails.map((e) => (
          <details class="card" style="margin-bottom:14px;border-radius:18px;">
            <summary style="cursor:pointer;">
              <span class="small" style="color:var(--sage-deep);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;">{e.day}</span><br />
              <span style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.45rem;">{e.subject}</span>
              <span class="small muted" style="display:block;">Preview: {e.preview}</span>
            </summary>
            <p style="white-space:pre-line;margin:16px 0;font-size:.98rem;">{e.body}</p>
            {e.buttons ? (
              <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;">
                {e.buttons.map(([label, href]) => <span class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost" style="pointer-events:none;">{label}</span><code class="small muted" style="word-break:break-all;">{href}</code>)}
              </div>
            ) : <span class="btn btn-sm btn-dark" style="pointer-events:none;">{e.cta}</span>}
            {e.rule && <div class="note peach" style="margin:16px 0 0;"><p class="small"><strong>Automation:</strong> {e.rule}</p></div>}
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
  <section class="band cream" id="setup">
    <div class="narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Setting up the Calm Nights pathway</span>
      <h2>How the automation works</h2>
      <hr class="divider" />
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Purchase → tag.</strong> Connect Stripe to your email platform (natively, or with a Zapier “Checkout Session completed” trigger). When metadata <code>packageId</code> is <code>calm-nights</code> or <code>calm-nights-bundle</code>, add the subscriber with tag <code>cn-buyer</code>; that starts Sequence 3. Any 1:1 <code>packageId</code> (<code>starter-*</code>, <code>standard-*</code>, …) adds tag <code>client</code>, which exits Sequences 3 and 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Check-in clicks → tags.</strong> Set a link-click trigger for each check-in URL. <code>s=support</code> adds <code>cn-support</code> (starts Sequence 4). <code>s=adjust</code> adds <code>cn-adjust</code>; a second “adjust” click also adds <code>cn-support</code>. <code>started=1</code> adds <code>cn-started</code> and starts the nights timer. Night 14 <code>s=on-track</code> adds <code>cn-success</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>One branch at a time.</strong> While a subscriber has <code>cn-support</code>, skip the remaining Sequence 3 check-ins after night 7 so they hear one clear message.</li>
        <li><strong>Measurement is built in.</strong> The check-in page records a GA4 event <code>calm_nights_checkin</code> (night, status), and every coaching link carries <code>?from=calm-nights</code>, so you can see how many Calm Nights families reach the pricing page. These feed the review on the <a href="/assets/flywheel#review">flywheel page</a>.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="note"><p><strong>Merge tag:</strong> replace <code>{'{first_name}'}</code> with your platform’s tag. The quiz, the Gentle Sleep Reset form and Stripe purchases add contacts to Brevo once its keys are set in Netlify — see the <a href="/assets/email-flow#setup">email flow setup checklist</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
